  "name": "Quadruped Band Fire Hydrant",
  "definition": "An all-fours unilateral bent-knee lateral lift against a mini band immediately above the knees, as shown by Boxing Science. The reviewed movement cue and still image establish hip abduction while the support knee and both hands stay planted. The source calls this an external-rotation exercise, but it does not show an axial femoral rotation path; hip rotation is therefore unreported in this contract. The pelvis and trunk are controlled without claiming zero measured motion. This quadruped fixture is distinct from side-lying, seated, and standing abduction. Band tension is non-comparable.",
